cervīcal  (cervīcāle ,
			Cassiod. Orth. p. 2302 P.),
			ālis, n.
		cervix, 
I.a pillow or bolster, = pulvinus;
				sing., Mart. 14,
				146; Juv. 6, 353;
				Petr. 56, 8;
			plur., Plin. Ep. 6, 16, 16;
					Petr. 32, 1; 78,
			5; Suet. Ner. 6; Plin. 20,
				20, 82, § 217; 28, 4, 12, §
